NNAAMMEE
     eennvv — set and print environment

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     eennvv [--ii] [--uu _n_a_m_e] [_n_a_m_e=_v_a_l_u_e _._._.] [_u_t_i_l_i_t_y [_a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t _._._.]]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     eennvv executes _u_t_i_l_i_t_y after modifying the environment as specified on the
     command line.  The option _n_a_m_e=_v_a_l_u_e specifies an environment variable,
     _n_a_m_e, with a value of _v_a_l_u_e.

     The options are as follows:

     --ii      Causes eennvv to completely ignore the environment it inherits.

     --uu _n_a_m_e
             Remove _n_a_m_e from the environment.

     If no _u_t_i_l_i_t_y is specified, eennvv prints out the names and values of the
     variables in the environment, with one _n_a_m_e=_v_a_l_u_e pair per line.

     eennvv doesn't handle commands with equal (‘=’) signs in their names, for
     obvious reasons.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The eennvv utility exits with one of the following values:

     0       eennvv completed successfully and, if _u_t_i_l_i_t_y was specified, it was
             invoked and completed successfully too.

     1       An invalid command line option was passed to eennvv and _u_t_i_l_i_t_y was
             not invoked, or _u_t_i_l_i_t_y was invoked but failed with exit status
             1.

     2–125, 128–255
             _u_t_i_l_i_t_y was invoked but failed with this exit status; see its
             manual page for more information.

     126     _u_t_i_l_i_t_y was found but could not be invoked, or it was invoked but
             failed with exit status 126.

     127     _u_t_i_l_i_t_y could not be found, or it was invoked but failed with
             exit status 127.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     execvp(3), environ(7)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The eennvv utility is compliant with the IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”)
     specification.  The flag [--uu] is an extension to that specification.

     The historic -- option has been deprecated but is still supported in this
     implementation.

